package:
  name: hdllint.vcs
  desc: VC Static lint integration (`vc_static_shell`)
  doc: |
    VC Static as a lint tool.  It runs in SpyGlass-compatible mode, so the
    report format, waiver syntax, and goal hierarchy are shared with the
    SpyGlass backend.

    What it sees: both the synthesis subset (RTL) and source-level style
    rules.  It implements the `Rtl` and `Style` families.

    `vc_static_shell` is invoked with a generated TCL script that sets the
    goal, reads the design, runs the checks, and writes a report.

    Profiles map to VC Static goals as:

    | profile   | goal                 |
    |-----------|----------------------|
    | `basic`   | `lint_turbo_rtl`     |
    | `default` | `lint_rtl`           |
    | `strict`  | `lint_rtl_enhanced`  |

    VC Static is the property of its respective owners.

  imports:
  - name: hdllint

  tasks:
  - export: Rtl
    uses: hdllint.Rtl
    desc: Runs VC Static RTL lint and reports normalized findings
    doc: |
      The `hdllint.Rtl` family task with `tools:` pinned to VC Static.
      Identical in every other respect -- same waivers, same baseline, same
      reports.

      Use this when a flow wants VC Static specifically; use `hdllint.Rtl`
      when it wants whatever lint tools are available.

      ```yaml
      - name: lint
        uses: hdllint.vcs.Rtl
        needs: [rtl]
        with:
          top: [wb_dma_top]
          profile: strict
      ```
    with:
      tools:
        type: list
        value: [vcs]

  - export: Style
    uses: hdllint.Style
    desc: Runs VC Static style checks and reports normalized findings
    doc: |
      The `hdllint.Style` family task with `tools:` pinned to VC Static.

      ```yaml
      - name: style
        uses: hdllint.vcs.Style
        needs: [rtl]
        with:
          top: [wb_dma_top]
      ```
    with:
      tools:
        type: list
        value: [vcs]
